# Ship live

A user-facing change is not done until the host that serves it is updated. Do this in the same turn, from the Stickitout repo root. Do not leave it for a later deploy.

- Marketing (`src/`, `public/`): `npm run shipit`. Confirm https://stickitoutdrums.com/.
- Member and admin (`workers/app`): `npm run portal:deploy`. That one deploy updates both https://member.stickitoutdrums.com/ and https://admin.stickitoutdrums.com/. Apply a new D1 migration first when the new code needs it.
- Analyzer (`analyzer/`): bump the static cache query (`?v=`) on `index.html`, the portal script tag in `workers/app/src/analyze.ts`, and every module import those files pull in. Then restart the server on port 8800 from `analyzer/` so https://analyzer-origin.stickitoutdrums.com/ serves this tree, and run `npm run portal:deploy` in the same turn. The member Analyze screen is the analyzer's `<main>`, fetched live by the Worker. A portal deploy alone does not change that HTML. Leave the named tunnel running. Do not print the access key. Confirm the origin returns the new markup (`CF-Cache-Status: DYNAMIC`). Logged-out `member.stickitoutdrums.com` is a 303 to `/login`.

Update `docs/source-of-truth.md` to `live` only after that ship succeeds. A file saved on this PC is not live.

Do not commit or git-push unless asked. Shipping is the deploy, not a git push.
